(A thing holds a list, a map and a buffer as fields. Each is declared with
 the literal a variable of its type is declared with, and is read, changed,
 walked and printed through the possessive the way the variable would be.)

A thing called note has
  a text called title is "shopping",
  a list called items is ["eggs"],
  a list called done,
  a map called counts is {"eggs": 6},
  a map called prices,
  a buffer called body is "milk",
  a buffer called scratch is 4 bytes in size.

a note called errand.
Print errand.

append "bread" to errand's items.
append 3.5 to errand's done.
Set errand's counts's "bread" to 1.
Set errand's prices's "milk" to 2.
append " and honey" to errand's body.
copy "abcdef" to errand's scratch.
On error Print "the scratch buffer holds four bytes".
Print errand.

Print errand's items's length.
Print errand's items's first.
Print errand's items's last.
Print element 2 of errand's items.
Set element 1 of errand's items to "duck eggs".
For each item in errand's items, Print item.
For each key in errand's counts's keys, Print key.
a number called eggs is errand's counts's "eggs".
Print eggs.
Print byte 1 of errand's body.
Set byte 1 of errand's body to 'M'.
Print errand's body.
Print errand's body's size.
If errand's done is empty then, Print "nothing done". Otherwise, Print "something done".
Print "items {errand's items} and counts {errand's counts}".
a text called summary is "body {errand's body}, {errand's items's length} items".
Print summary.

(A field written whole takes its own copy of what it is given.)
a list called fresh is [1, 2].
Set errand's done to fresh.
append 3 to fresh.
Print errand's done.
Print fresh.
errand's prices is {"tea": 4}.
Set errand's body to "{errand's title}!".
Print errand.

(A field read out whole into a variable is the variable's own copy.)
a list called taken is errand's items.
append "only taken" to taken.
a map called counted is errand's counts.
Set counted's "only counted" to 0.
a buffer called copied is errand's body.
append "?" to copied.
Print errand.
Print taken.
Print counted.
Print copied.
To 'the items'.
  Return a list, errand's items.

a list called returned is 'the items'.
append "only returned" to returned.
Print errand's items.
Print returned.

(A list parameter is the caller's list, so a field grows through one.)
To 'stock up' with a list called shelf.
  append each count from 1 to 20 to shelf.

'stock up' with errand's done.
Print errand's done's length.

(Free releases a field's list or buffer, which reads empty afterwards.)
Free errand's items.
Print errand's items.
append "after" to errand's items.
On error Print "a freed list refuses an append".
Free errand's body.
Free errand's body.
On error Print "a second Free sets the error flag".
Print errand's body's size.
